{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the magicians did so with their secret arts to bring out the lice:</b> It says <b>\"and they did so\"</b> — that they struck the dust of the earth and adjured the demons by oath, and performed their secret arts as they had done on other occasions to bring out the lice, but they could not. And it is possible that \"and they did so\" teaches that they did the proper procedure that brings out the lice, but their efforts did not succeed this time, for the wise men among the magicians knew what was within the power of their hand to do, and they had already tested their methods in this manner on other occasions."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Reading בלטיהם/לטיהם as \"their secret arts\" (cf. לטים, occult arts); Ramban appears to distinguish between demonic adjuration and technical procedures as two possible readings of what the magicians attempted."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:04:55.236596039Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}